# Pairs with RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog, and reproduces issue #4523 end to end as
# production has it: a never-written leaf with no snapshot releases at its
# persisted checkpoint; a cold rebuild (the first fault, a leaf stop) captures a
# snapshot below that release; the GC trims past it; and the next activation (the
# second fault) rehydrates the low snapshot and latches stale. It needs two faults,
# so the mutation raises the fault budget to two - the base configuration's one
# hid the defect. The base keeps the block until coverage exists.
MODULE: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLogNoSnapshotReleaseTwoFaults
TARGET: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a never-written leaf releases above any coverage, and a later low cold-rebuild snapshot latches it stale after the trim
PERTURBS: PublishPin

--- FIND
          THEN MergePin(l, "zero", NeverWrittenRelease(l))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: with no snapshot the release is the persisted checkpoint.
          THEN MergePin(l, "zero", IF cov[l] < 0 THEN stCp[l] ELSE NeverWrittenRelease(l))
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the defect needs two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END